Package: aquaTrajectories
Title: Aquatic Animal Movement and Multiview Trajectories
Version: 0.2.1
Authors@R: person("Stefanos", "Balaskas", email = "s.balaskas@ac.upatras.gr", role = c("aut", "cre"), comment = c(ORCID = "0000-0003-2444-9796"))
Description: Provides functions to import and validate time-stamped two- and three-dimensional aquatic-animal trajectories; compute swimming and group movement measures; align trajectories to experimental events; and compare detections and track identities with external reference annotations. Implements camera synchronization, calibration-aware multiview reconstruction, refractive geometry, trajectory models, and conditional measurement-error scenarios. Optional integration scripts support externally configured video trackers. Provides source-preserving trajectory quality-control, estimator sensitivity, measurement-unit contracts, checks of independent experimental units, spatial-support diagnostics, geometry-association and placebo analyses, and reproducible evidence reports. Simulated movement and software benchmarks cannot independently establish biological identities, physical underwater accuracy, causal feeding effects or welfare outcomes.
